"""
Parameters shared by every analysis that builds a synchronous program and runs it on the
QUBE: how to build it, whether and where to run it, and what to watch it with.

Both analyses in this library extend this one. They differ in the program they build and in
what they do with the log afterwards — running it is the same job, and the four targets
below are available to both:

| `export_c` | `deploy_host` | what happens                                                |
|------------|---------------|-------------------------------------------------------------|
| false      | empty         | the program is built in-process on `backend` and ticked from Julia |
| true       | empty         | standalone C is written to `output_dir`, compiled and run there   |
| either     | set           | the C sources are copied to that host, built and run there, and the log is streamed and fetched back |

A named `deploy_host` therefore implies `export_c`: an in-process run happens in the Julia
process, so it cannot happen on another machine, and C sources are the only thing there is to
send. Setting the host is enough.

`run = false` stops before any of that, which is how a program is built and checked, or an
earlier log re-analyzed, without a device attached.

The log is always written by the program itself (a `DataLogger` inside it), so the same
columns come out of every target and nothing in the loop around it writes data.
"""
partial analysis QubeHardwareRunBase
  extends Analysis
  model::Dyad.EmptyComponent = Dyad.EmptyComponent()
  "Sample time [s]"
  parameter Ts::Real = 0.005
  "Run the program on the hardware; false only builds it"
  parameter run::Boolean = false
  "Duration [s] of the run; 0 means the program's own natural length"
  parameter Tf::Real = 0.0
  "Motor saturation [V]"
  parameter umax::Real = 10.0
  """
  Arm angle [deg] at start-up, added to every shoulder reading, so the arm need not be at
  its home position first
  """
  parameter arm_deg::Real = 0.0
  """
  Card-specific options applied after opening the board, e.g.
  \"deadband_compensation=0.0\". Empty leaves the driver on its own defaults
  """
  parameter card_options::String = "deadband_compensation=0.0"
  """
  Backend to build the program on when it runs in-process, \"julia\" or \"c\". Ignored when
  `export_c` is true, which always builds C
  """
  parameter backend::String = "julia"
  "Export the program as standalone C into `output_dir`, and run that instead of in-process"
  parameter export_c::Boolean = false
  "Directory the generated C sources and the log are written to"
  parameter output_dir::String = "furuta_c"
  """
  File the program writes its log to. Passed to the `DataLogger` inside the model *and* used
  to open the file, so the two cannot disagree. Empty keeps the program's own default name.
  Exported and deployed runs use the bare file name inside their own directory, since an
  absolute path from this machine means nothing on the target
  """
  parameter log_file::String = ""
  """
  Host to build and run on, e.g. \"username@hostname\"; empty runs on this machine. Implies
  `export_c`, since C sources are what gets copied over
  """
  parameter deploy_host::String = ""
  "Directory on `deploy_host` to copy the sources into"
  parameter deploy_dir::String = "furuta_c"
  "Launch a live plotter alongside the run to watch it as it happens (needs `run = true`)"
  parameter live_plot::Boolean = false
  "Live-plot viewer executable"
  parameter live_plot_cmd::String = "kst2"
  "Viewer session file; a relative path resolves against `output_dir`"
  parameter live_plot_config::String = "kst2config.kst"
relations
end